{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>For you have found favor, etc.</b> Now Moses preceded by saying <b>יְדַעְתִּיךָ בְּשֵׁם</b> (I have known You by name), and afterward said <b>and also I have found favor</b>. Here Scripture informs him that the attainment of knowledge in the Name is higher than the aspect of attaining favor, for Noah found favor in the eyes of HaShem (Genesis 6:8) yet did not know Him in the Name. Therefore He said first <b>you have found favor in My eyes</b> — and not this alone, but also <b>and I have known you by Name.</b>" "<b>Further,</b> it intends to say to him that what He made known to him in the Name was also on account of his having found favor in His eyes. Therefore He preceded by saying <b>you have found favor in My eyes</b> and afterward <b>and I have known you by Name</b> — to say that this proceeded from that. Unlike what is heard from Moses' words, where he preceded ״יְדַעְתִּיךָ בְשֵׁם״ before the finding of favor — which would indicate that he attained the thing on account of what he had merited."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:36:27.290225323Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}